> me is telling me that loot=currency=win... but burdened is bad... help?

Nethack is not AD&D, nor FFVII, nor any other RPG (pencil-and-paper,
or computer-game) you've played. Habits and instincts from those other
games don't translate well.

Being burdened is bad because it makes you slower. Monsters get to do
more stuff (like hit you!) for each move you get.

So? So, carry less stuff and/or increase the amount of stuff you can
carry without being burdened.

To start with, divide your stuff into sets along the lines of "need
to have it ready for instant use", "will need at some future point but
no time pressure" and "unlikely to ever be useful unless something
bizarre happens". Only carry stuff in the first category.

Learn what the different containers do and use them effectively.
Container use is the key to effective loot management, and helps you
in other ways as well.

> Less importantly, does anyone have any useful advice about controls?

Stick with hjkl, and learn the diagonals (yubn) that go with it. You'll
be way happier in the long run. You don't have to move your fingers off
the home rows nearly as often, for starters. You'll also be able to play
on the better sorts of keyboards (like the Happy Hacking Lite 2, or the
awe-inspiring BTC-5100 mini, neither of which has a numeric keypad), and
on laptops.

> picking up huge piles of loot when meaning to fight something...  ^^;

Use '@' to toggle autopickup, and set your autopickup types to something
conservative. I generally set mine to $"=/?! when starting out, and
turn off frequently (e.g. in shops or during my run).

Also on the topic of controls, use Ctrl-<dir> to travel, not
Shift-<dir> or m-<dir>. Much safer. Make it a habit to make one move,
observe the result, think, _then_ make the next move.

